; One variable: whether the text is taller than the rect. A RichTextLabel with scroll_active true
; shows its vertical scrollbar and wraps its text beside it once the text exceeds the rect height
; (rich_text_label.cpp:3801-3830). Each label has the same text and width. Overflow is shorter than
; its text and shows the bar; ScrollInactive is the same box with scroll_active false and shows
; none; Fits is tall enough for its text and shows none. No other RichTextLabel fixture sets
; scroll_active true with text that exceeds its rect, so no other scene shows a regression in it.

